      {
       "type": "narrate",
       "style": "chat",
       "requires_flags": [
        "flag/name-nobody"
       ],
       "text": "The hills answer him. His own kind call in at the stone: \"Polyphemus! Who is killing you?\" And he roars his ruined face against the rock: \"NOBODY! Nobody is killing me!\" A pause. Then, going away up the mountain: \"If nobody hurts you, it is a sickness from Zeus. Pray to your father.\" And the footsteps do not come back. He hears them go."
      },
      {
       "type": "narrate",
       "style": "chat",
       "requires_flags": [
        "flag/name-boast"
       ],
       "text": "The hills answer him. His own kind call in: \"Polyphemus! Who has done this?\" And he roars back the name you laid down over the wine, whole and proud: \"ODYSSEUS! Sacker of cities, son of Laertes, of Ithaca — he was under my roof!\" And they believe him. \"Hold, cousin — we cannot shift your stone from without. Wait for the light; at dawn every hand on the mountain opens it together.\" Perimedes has your sleeve: \"They come back at dawn, Captain. We leave before they do.\""
      },
      {
       "type": "narrate",
       "style": "chat",
       "requires_flags": [
        "flag/name-lie"
       ],
       "text": "The hills answer him. His own kind call in: \"Polyphemus! Who has done this?\" And he roars back the name you gave him over the wine: \"AITHON! A Cretan, out of Crete — at my own fire!\" A silence. Then, cool and turning away: \"A Cretan. Cousin, the Cretans lie; it is the one thing known of them. Sleep it off.\" And the footsteps go, half-convinced of nothing, and do not come back tonight."
      },
